cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  dMRI Rosetta Stone: An Open-Source Interactive Platform for
  Cross-Tool Diffusion MRI Education and Reproducibility
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Busra
    family-names: Mutlu
    affiliation: King's College London
repository-code: 'https://github.com/happybrotherhood/dmri-rosetta-stone'
abstract: >-
  An open-source, containerised platform that presents the same
  diffusion MRI operation in FSL, MRtrix3, and DIPY side by side,
  executable on real open human brain data. Covers seven canonical
  pipeline stages from brain extraction through tractography and
  voxelwise group analysis. Ships with a reproducible benchmark of
  inter-tool agreement across two independent open datasets.
keywords:
  - diffusion MRI
  - FSL
  - MRtrix3
  - DIPY
  - educational software
  - neuroinformatics
  - reproducibility
  - open science
license: MIT
